<script>
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import ContractPages from './lib/ContractPages.abide'
import contractPages from './lib/ContractPages.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import DimLastArrow from './lib/DimLastArrow.abide'
import dimLastArrow from './lib/DimLastArrow.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import FullScreenPages from './lib/FullScreenPages.abide'
import fullScreenPages from './lib/FullScreenPages.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/headless/carousel', '/headless/dialog', '/behaviors/hotkeys']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/ContractViewer.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a page picked opens the viewer on it, and the arrows step it'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/lightbox.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the arrow keys step it as its carousel buttons do"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/lightbox.test.ts',
            from: ['test("its backdrop is its dialog\'s'],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Open a contract's pages on the one picked">
        <p>A lightbox is a <code>carousel</code> inside a <code>dialog</code>, its arrow keys
            bound with <code>hotkeys</code> to the carousel's own <code>previous</code> and
            <code>next</code>. Spread <code>dialog</code> on a <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> and
            the carousel's parts inside it, and call <code>show(key)</code> to open it resting on
            that item. Escape and the backdrop close it, as they do any dialog.</p>
        <Example code={contractPages}><ContractPages /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Close a full-screen contract viewer on a click beside the page">
        <p>A lightbox filling the screen has no backdrop outside its box. Spread
            <code>backdrop</code> on the element around the pages: a click on it, and not on a
            page, closes the lightbox.</p>
        <Example code={fullScreenPages}><FullScreenPages /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Dim the arrow that has no page beyond">
        <p><code>previous</code> is disabled on the first page and <code>next</code> on the last.</p>
        <Example code={dimLastArrow}><DimLastArrow /></Example>
    </Section>
</Doc>
